course: dictionary
lesson: 11662
title: Aspirate: the puff of breath
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To aspirate a sound means to say it with a small puff of breath. Hold your hand in front of your mouth and say «pin». You feel a puff on your hand after the p. That puff is aspiration. Now say «spin». The p has no puff, so it is not aspirated.
explain: Aspirate can be a verb or a noun. «The teacher asked us to aspirate the p in pin.» Here it is a verb, an action. «An aspirate is a sound with a puff of air, like the h in hat.» Here it is a noun, a thing. Check the word around it to see which one it is.
explain: In medicine, aspirate is a different meaning. «The nurse had to aspirate the fluid from his knee with a needle.» It means to suck something out with a tube or needle. Another meaning is to breathe food or liquid into the lungs by accident, which is why choking is dangerous.
fact: To aspirate a sound means to say it with a puff of breath.
fact: The h in «hat» and the p in «pin» are aspirated sounds.
fact: The p in «spin» is not aspirated, because the s comes before it.
fact: In medicine, to aspirate means to suck something out with a tube or needle.
fact: In Mandarin pinyin, p is aspirated but b is not, so the two sounds are told apart by the puff.
exercise: When you say «pin», which sound gets the puff of breath? | *The p at the start | There is no puff in pin | The i in the middle | The n at the end
exercise: «The nurse used a needle to aspirate fluid from his knee.» What does aspirate mean here? | *Suck the fluid out with a needle | Rub it with cream | Burst the skin open | Warm it up with a towel
exercise: Which sentence uses aspirate as a noun? | *An h at the start of hat is an aspirate | The doctor will aspirate the fluid today | We aspirated the sound together | The teacher will aspirate the sound in pin
test: Which word starts with an aspirated p, with a puff of breath? | sping | spin | *pin | ps
test: What is it called when food or liquid is breathed into the lungs by accident? | To sneeze loudly | *To aspirate | To whisper | To yawn
exam: In Mandarin pinyin, which sound is aspirated, with a puff of breath? | Neither | *p | Both p and b | b
